# /<COMMAND_NAME>

> **What this is.** A slash command at `.claude/commands/<COMMAND_NAME>.md`. Invoked by typing `/<COMMAND_NAME>` in Claude Code. The command's body is treated as a prompt; pre-flight inline-bash (`!\`...\``) executes BEFORE the prompt runs and its output becomes context.
>
> **Why slash commands matter.** They turn repeated multi-step workflows into single keystrokes. The pre-flight pattern (inline bash that pre-computes context) avoids back-and-forth tool calls within the command, dramatically reducing latency.

Pre-flight context (auto-collected; the values below are interpolated before the prompt body runs):

- **<CONTEXT_LABEL_1>:** !`<BASH_COMMAND_1>`
- **<CONTEXT_LABEL_2>:** !`<BASH_COMMAND_2>`
- **<CONTEXT_LABEL_3>:** !`<BASH_COMMAND_3>`
- **<CONTEXT_LABEL_4>:** !`<BASH_COMMAND_4>`

User-provided argument (may be empty): $ARGUMENTS

